<title>FINLAND: Enso 1996 profit falls 53 percent.</title>
<headline>Enso 1996 profit falls 53 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to Dec 31-</p>
<p>					   (million markka unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after financial items		 1,665 vs 3,523</p>
<p> Earnings per share (markka)		   4.50 vs 10.52</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (markka)		    1.80 vs 2.02</p>
<p> Net sales					 25,660 vs 28,026</p>
<p> Operating profit				 2,706 vs 4,933</p>
<p>NOTE - The median of analysts' forecast had been for a 1996 profit before extras of 1,575 million markka (mean 1,563 million) in a 1,311 to 1,728 million markka range.  </p>
<p> Net financial items		   charge 1,041 vs 1,410 charge</p>
<p> Extraordinary items			 gain 173 vs 94 charge</p>
<p> Profit before appropriations, taxes	1,838 vs 3,429</p>
<p>Increase in accumulated</p>
<p>  depreciation			     charge 732 vs 1,616 charge</p>
<p> Direct taxes for the period		    272 vs 207</p>
<p> Direct taxes for previous periods	gain 24 vs 35 charge</p>
<p> Profit before minorities		     1,051 vs 1,747</p>
<p> Minorities				   charge 17 vs 10 charge</p>
<p> Net profit					1,033  vs 1,737</p>
<p> Equity to assets ratio (percent)	    42.1 vs 39.3</p>
<p>@</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Finnish forest industry group is Enso Oy.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +35 89 6805 0245</p>
</text>
